["A fictional equilibrium population contains a rare dominant allele. Which statement is correct?","dominance does not require a high allele frequency","dominance forces its frequency above one half","recessive alleles cannot be common","Dominance describes expression in heterozygotes and places no lower bound on how common the allele must be."],
["A small fictional sample differs slightly from Hardy–Weinberg expectations. What should an analysis consider before rejecting the model?","random sampling variation and statistical evidence","whether the dominant allele has the longest name","that any nonzero discrepancy proves adaptation","Observed samples fluctuate, so statistical evaluation is needed before attributing a discrepancy to a biological mechanism."]
